━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ AIQuestionToolkit
    is AIToolkit

╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌ is AIToolkit ╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌

────────────────────
+ tools [AITool]

List'AITool([ai-question-tool()])

────────────────────
+ context String?
    - request AIRequest

ai-question-note()

────────────────────
+ run AIToolkitResult ?! Error
    - request AIRequest
    - call AIToolCallPart

?! AIError(AIErrorKind.invalid-request, "There is no tool named ${call.tool-name}")
    if !ai-is-question-call(call)
?! AIError(AIErrorKind.invalid-request, "$ai-question-tool-name needs a question and at least one choice with a label")
    if !ai-question(call)

AIToolkitResult(ai-question-shown)

╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ ai-is-question-call Bool
    - call AIToolCallPart

call.tool-name == ai-question-tool-name

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ do ai-question AIQuestion?
    - call AIToolCallPart

=? null if !ai-is-question-call(call)
. fields = match? call.arguments
    | [String = JSON]
=? null if !fields
. text = ai-question-text(fields["question"])
=? null if !text
. listed = match? fields["choices"]
    | [JSON]
. choices = List'AIQuestionChoice()
for value in listed ?? List'JSON()
    . choice = match? value
        | [String = JSON]
    . label = ai-question-text(choice?["label"])
    if label && choices.length < ai-question-choice-limit
        choices += AIQuestionChoice(label, ai-question-text(choice?["detail"]))
=? null if !choices
= AIQuestion(text, ai-question-text(fields["context"]), choices)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ do ai-reply-question AIQuestion?
    - parts [AIMessagePart]

. index = parts.length
while index > 0
    index -= 1
    if | call AIToolCallPart = parts[index]
        . found = ai-question(call)
        =? found if found
= null

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ do ai-reply-asks Bool
    - parts [AIMessagePart]

=? true if ai-reply-question(parts)
. index = parts.length
while index > 0
    index -= 1
    if | part AITextPart = parts[index]
        . closing = ai-closing-text(part.text)
        =? closing.ends-with("?") if closing.length > 0
= false

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ do ai-closing-text String
    - text String

. closing = text.trim()
while closing.ends-with("*") || closing.ends-with("_")
    closing = closing[0 .. < closing.length - 1].trim()
= closing

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ai-question-text String?
    - value JSON?

match? value
    | text String {it.trim().length > 0}
        text.trim()

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ai-question-tool AITool

AITool(ai-question-tool-name, ai-question-description(), parameters)

.. parameters = Map'String'JSON
    • type "object"
    • properties Map'String'JSON
        • question Map'String'JSON
            • type "string"
            • description "The one decision, in at most 100 characters: never two decisions joined by “and”, and no reason, recommendation, or list of the choices"
        • context Map'String'JSON
            • type "string"
            • description "One or two sentences the person needs in order to decide, or an empty string when the question stands on its own"
        • choices Map'String'JSON
            • type "array"
            • description "One or two answers, your recommendation first. Add a second only when it is a realistic alternative the person might pick instead, not a menu of everything you mentioned."
            • items ai-question-choice-schema()
    • required ai-question-required()
    • "additionalProperties" false

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ai-question-choice-schema JSON

Map'String'JSON
    • type "object"
    • properties Map'String'JSON
        • label Map'String'JSON
            • type "string"
            • description "The answer in the person's own words, one to three words, such as “Yes, fix it” or “Not now”. Choosing it sends these words to you as their reply."
        • detail Map'String'JSON
            • type "string"
            • description "What choosing it leads to, in one short line, or an empty string"
    • required ai-question-choice-required()
    • "additionalProperties" false

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ai-question-required [JSON]

* "question"
* "context"
* "choices"

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ai-question-choice-required [JSON]

* "label"
* "detail"

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ¶ ai-question-description

Shows the person one question about what happens next, as choices under your reply.
Call it once, when your work for the turn is done and before your closing message, only when the next move is the person's call: a choice between approaches, a go-ahead for a next step you recommend, or an approval.
Most turns need none. Do not ask about work that belongs to the task; do it.
Do not offer speculative extras, and do not repeat an offer the person passed over unless what it acts on has changed.
It does not wait for an answer: the person's choice arrives as their next message.
After calling it, write your closing message: your full answer, as the last thing in the turn. Never write that answer before the call, and do not mention the question or repeat its choices.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ¶ ai-question-note

<next-step>
When this turn leaves the person a decision that is theirs to make, such as a choice between approaches, a go-ahead for a next step you recommend, or an approval, ask it with the $ai-question-tool-name tool rather than in your reply, loading the tool first if it is deferred.
Most turns leave none. Don't ask about work that belongs to the task; do it. Don't offer speculative extras, and don't repeat an offer the person passed over.
Call it once your work is done and before your closing message, then write your full answer as the last thing in the turn, without mentioning the question.
</next-step>
